# A lacuna type that is not a literal: Translate checks it against thema's lacuna types, so it must be known from the lens.
-- source.cue --
a!: int
t!: string
-- target.cue --
b!: int
-- lens.cue --
v0_0: _
v1_0: {b: v0_0.a}
lacunas: [{
	sourceFields: [{path: "a", value: v0_0.a}]
	message: "m"
	type:    v0_0.t
}]
-- out --
not total
lacunas[0].type is v0_0.t, which is not a literal; write a lacuna's type as one of thema's lacuna types, as a string or as thema.LacunaTypes.<name> (rule not-a-value) @ lens.cue:6:11
